  "dom_id": "step-q94641",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{-6y},\\, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $Y$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le m) & ={\\int }_{0}^{m}6{e}^{-6y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6y}{|}_{0}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-6m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{-6m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -6m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ -6m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
